# LCV-175 AC 3, AC 8 — an Illustrator-style file: the colors live in a
# `<defs><style>` sheet of classes. `.cls-1` strokes red, `.cls-2` blue; the
# `g .cls-2` rule has a descendant combinator, so it is dropped and reported,
# and the nested line stays blue. No layer is declared and all geometry is
# colored: one `#rrggbb` layer per color in order of first appearance, no `Cut`.
# The `<defs>` holds only the `<style>`, so it is not reported.
# World y = 80 - svg y.
bed 100 80
layer "#ff0000" #ff0000 output=1 current=1
layer "#0000ff" #0000ff output=1
line 0 10 70 90 70
circle 1 50 40 15
line 1 10 10 90 10
ignored 1 style rule (unsupported selector)
